If you don't want to run statd and lockd (which take no CPU time unless
someone talks to them), then you should purge your system of all programs
that do file locking or stop using NFS.

I'm not certain about Ultrix, but some mail programs use file locking
to ensure they don't miss any mail.  If this applies to your system, then
be sure to tell you community to not access mail files over NFS.

BTW, Ultrix questions are best sent to comp.unix.ultrix.
