In <3ppna0$50p@hpg30a.csc.cuhk.hk> kpwong@psy.cuhk.hk (Kit-pui Wong) writes:
>I am a fresh sysadmin on AlphaStation.
>After last time I logout from the console, I can never login again, with
>my own account and the root account.
>When I login my user account, the console reported something like
>"user limit exceeds" but there is actually no user logging in.
>When I tried to login as root, it reported "invalid login"
>        kpwong@psy.cuhk.hk
>Thanks!
>KiT

Sound to me like license PAK problems.
When you first set up the machine, you must enter the software license PAK
for OSF-BASE that comes with the machine. Boot up into single user mode,
then run the license manager to register it:

OSF> lmf register

Fill in the details from the PAK. OSF-BASE comes with an implicit 2 user
license. This is the number of different users that can be logged on at once.
eg you can have 2 root logins, and 3 logins for user "fred", but if user
"barney" tries to log in, it will fail.

Mark.

